# Cloudspire Skycycle: its enters trigger needs another Vehicle or creature "you control" (CR 115.1, 109.5). On turn three Bot1 casts it (Mox
# Ruby, Mox Pearl and Black Lotus) while the only other creature is Bot2's Memnite: the Skycycle is not its own target and the Memnite is not
# Bot1's, so the trigger has no legal target and is never put on the stack (CR 603.3d); the Memnite stays 1/1. Bot1 then casts its own Memnite
# and crews the Vehicle with it - Crew 1, a power of exactly 1 - which makes it an artifact creature, with its printed flying.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Memnite
Cloudspire Skycycle
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Island x19

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cloudspire Skycycle.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield.Cloudspire Skycycle.Types = Artifact
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Cloudspire Skycycle.Activate(Ability: Crew)
Bot1.Choose(Memnite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Cloudspire Skycycle.Types = Artifact; Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Cloudspire Skycycle.Keywords = Flying
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = true
